# CareLoop local configuration — TEMPLATE. Copy to `.env` and fill in.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# `.env` is ignored by git (`.gitignore` ignores `.env` and `.env.*`, and negates this file
# alone). Verified with `git check-ignore -v .env`, not by reading the pattern. Never commit a
# populated copy, and never paste a key into a conversation, an issue or a commit message.
#
# Nothing under `careloop/` or `tests/` reads this file. The default test suite runs entirely on
# the mock model provider, at $0, with zero secrets configured — CI proves it, since CI has none.
# Only the benchmark harness under `bench/` loads these values.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# AWS — Bedrock (Nova Lite, Nova Micro)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Use a DEDICATED IAM USER for this, not root credentials and not an admin key. The benchmark
# needs exactly three actions, and an inline policy granting only these is enough:
#
#   bedrock:InvokeModel             the actual model calls
#   bedrock:ListFoundationModels    enumerating what the account can reach
#   sts:GetCallerIdentity           confirming which principal is in use before spending
#
# Root credentials cannot be scoped, cannot be rotated without disruption, and cannot be revoked
# in isolation if they leak. A dedicated user can be deleted outright.
#
# Region matters: Bedrock model availability is per-region, and the model id below is a
# region-prefixed inference profile (see CARELOOP_BEDROCK_MODEL_ID).
AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=
AWS_DEFAULT_REGION=us-east-1

# Only for temporary credentials (STS / SSO / assumed role). Leave blank for a long-lived IAM
# user key pair. If set, it expires — a probe that worked yesterday failing today with
# ExpiredTokenException means this, not a quota change.
AWS_SESSION_TOKEN=

# Full override of the Bedrock model id. Bedrock uses region-prefixed inference-profile ids
# (`us.` / `eu.` / `apac.`); the bare `amazon.nova-lite-v1:0` fails on accounts that require a
# profile. Leave blank to let providers.py derive the prefix from the resolved region.
CARELOOP_BEDROCK_MODEL_ID=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OpenAI
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# This key holds a small, non-replaceable balance. `bench/run.py` prints an estimated cost and
# refuses to make a paid call without an explicit --confirm-spend flag; responses are cached to
# disk so re-running an unchanged task set costs nothing.
OPENAI_API_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NVIDIA — hosted models via the OpenAI-compatible path
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Same provider class as OpenAI, pointed at a different base_url. Keys come from build.nvidia.com.
NVIDIA_API_KEY=
NVIDIA_BASE_URL=https://integrate.api.nvidia.com/v1

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Model selection per role
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Which model backs each role. Unset means the mock provider, which is the default everywhere and
# is the only model the test suite ever sees. Set these only to point CareLoop at a real endpoint.
#
# Spec form:  mock                        the scripted mock provider
#             bedrock                     model id derived from the region prefix
#             bedrock:<model-id>          explicit model id
#             openai:<model>              OpenAI proper, key from OPENAI_API_KEY
#             openai:<model>@<base_url>   any OpenAI-compatible gateway, key from OPENAI_API_KEY
#             nvidia:<model>              NVIDIA hosted, key from NVIDIA_API_KEY, base from
#                                         NVIDIA_BASE_URL
#
# `nvidia` is the same OpenAI-compatible provider class with a different credential source. It
# gets its own prefix rather than being written as `openai:<model>@<nvidia url>` because the key
# to use would then have to be guessed from the host, and a benchmark that silently sends the
# wrong key produces an auth error that reads like a model failure.
#
# Examples:   CARELOOP_MODEL_TRIAGE=bedrock:us.amazon.nova-micro-v1:0
#             CARELOOP_MODEL_PLANNER=openai:gpt-4o-mini
#             CARELOOP_MODEL_EXTRACTION=nvidia:meta/llama-3.3-70b-instruct
#
# An unrecognised spec raises at resolution. It does NOT fall back to the mock: a run that looks
# real, costs nothing and proves nothing is the worst available failure mode.
#
# MEASURED DEFAULTS, from docs/model-benchmark.md (2026-08-11, 20 tasks, 6 candidates):
#
#   CARELOOP_MODEL_TRIAGE=bedrock:us.amazon.nova-micro-v1:0
#   CARELOOP_MODEL_PLANNER=bedrock:us.amazon.nova-2-lite-v1:0
#   CARELOOP_MODEL_EXTRACTION=bedrock:us.amazon.nova-2-lite-v1:0
#
# Note what is NOT recommended: `bedrock:us.amazon.nova-lite-v1:0`. It was the intended primary
# until it was measured. Given an explicit booking instruction alongside a document asking for
# something else, it proposed emailing the document's address instead. The policy engine denies
# that call, but there is no reason to pick the model that makes it.
#
# `openai:gpt-4o-mini` is the fallback and is within noise of Nova 2 Lite on planning.
#
# Left blank below on purpose: the library defaults to the mock, and the test suite must never see
# anything else. Set them in your own .env when running the real system.
CARELOOP_MODEL_TRIAGE=
CARELOOP_MODEL_PLANNER=
CARELOOP_MODEL_EXTRACTION=
